{
  "format": "call-of-slop-construct-part/1",
  "name": "Bake Oven",
  "description": "An Oven Core, the Recuperator: bakes a welded group of subparts in a roller hearth tunnel. Weld Oven Bed Blocks beside it (the bed is their rectangle, up to 32 x 32 m): the oven draws a tunnel over the bed, along the side the Core is welded to, with swing doors at both ends. A kit rolls in on a Roller Tile run that meets the end nearer the Core, the doors shut, it bakes, the doors open, and it rolls out along a run that starts at the far end (or waits for a crane or an arm). Its Tunnel height setting is the clear height over the rollers. Needs power.",
